            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Moving to Weimar</strong><br>\nIn 1708, Bach moved to Weimar, where he became a court organist and a concertmaster. During his time in Weimar, Bach composed many of his famous works, including organ concertos and cantatas. His tenure here marked the beginning of his prolific period as a composer.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Bach's Family Life</strong><br>\nBach married his second cousin, Maria Barbara Bach, in 1707, and together they had seven children, several of whom became significant musicians themselves. After Maria's death, Bach married Anna Magdalena Wilcke, a soprano who helped transcribe his music. Together, they had thirteen more children.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Köthen Period</strong><br>\nIn 1717, Bach moved to Köthen to serve as Kapellmeister for Prince Leopold. During this period, he focused on instrumental compositions, including his well-known Brandenburg Concertos. Prince Leopold's support and the relative freedom of court allowed Bach to compose some of his most important instrumental works.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
